    "bitcoin_integration": "Emerging but business-friendly framework: Vanuatu passed the Virtual Asset Service Providers (VASP) Act No. 3 of 2025 (passed 26 March 2025, in force 12 May 2025), which explicitly references Bitcoin and gives the VFSC licensing/supervision authority over crypto businesses (exchanges, custodians, token offerings, a fintech sandbox), aligning with FATF travel-rule and APG/IOSCO standards. Owning, buying, selling and using Bitcoin is legal for individuals, but crypto is NOT legal tender (the national currency is the vatu, VUV); the VFSC warns there is no statutory compensation for crypto losses and steers retail investors away without full risk awareness."
